WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.040
Film Courage: [George Orwell’s] In Nineteen
Eighty-Four, you said it was a book that would

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.700
be one of the five books you would take with
you if you couldn’t read any other books,

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.530
I’m curious why?

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:21.019
Bill Duke, filmmaker/actor/author: I’m going
to get in trouble for this but Nineteen Eighty-Four

00:00:21.019 --> 00:00:26.070
is something we’re living today…George
Orwell…it was one of my favorite books at

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:36.180
the time but when I’m looking at the film
and reading the book since this last election

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.850
and it has a section about the thought police.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.570
Have you guys ever read Nineteen Eighty-Four?

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:45.080
Film Courage: I know parts of it but have
not read it entirely.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.070
But I’ve heard the whole concept about the
thought police.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:55.640
Bill: The thought police in Nineteen Eighty-Four,
you are not allowed to do anything without

00:00:55.640 --> 00:01:06.479
the permission of the thought police and they
determine your reality.

00:01:06.479 --> 00:01:10.250
They create this war that is not really a
war that is happening at all.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:16.180
But they have these soldiers marching and
all this stuff…blah, blah, blah, blah.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.080
You’re not allowed to have a relationship
without their permission.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.640
You can’t just fall in love.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.079
You have to have their permission go through
them.

00:01:24.079 --> 00:01:33.360
So Richard Burton is the head of the thought
police [“O’Brien”] and John…[John

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:43.790
Hurt] he is a citizen and he and this woman
fall in love.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:48.530
They keep meeting secretly at her place and
his place and are running away.

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:53.930
One day they are caught by the thought police
and the helicopters come and the soldiers

00:01:53.930 --> 00:02:04.420
come and take them to the police headquarters
and John [John Hurt as Winston Smith] is lying

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:10.300
on the table of the thought police headquarters
and there’s a spotlight on the table and

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:17.730
he’s lying there naked with his hands tied
and his feet tied and this electrical force

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:22.390
comes through the table with a switch where
if you turn the switch on it electrocutes

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:26.680
you and there is water coming down.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:34.790
And so there’s a guy near the button and
Richard Burton is sitting there and John is

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:37.080
saying “I’m so sorry.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.080
I was wrong.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.690
I did it.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:42.860
I should have never, ever seen her.”

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:50.800
And then an image of Burton says “Well you
know, she said that you started it.”

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.920
“I don’t know, I’ll never do it again.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.470
Please forgive me.”

00:02:56.470 --> 00:03:01.210
And Richard Burton says “Shhh, it’s okay.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:06.870
I just want to trust but verify.”

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:17.300
So he says to John “How many fingers am
I holding up?”

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.580
And John says “Four.”

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:28.910
Richard Burton nods to the guy with the button
“Ahhh!!”

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:34.520
[Bill imitates John crying out].

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:39.000
Richard Burton says “Stop.”

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:45.130
“What did I do wrong?

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:49.980
What I do wrong?”

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:54.050
“How many fingers am I holding up.”

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:55.050
“Four.”

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:58.470
[Bill imitates Richard Burton and nods to
begin shocking John].

00:03:58.470 --> 00:03:59.470
“Ahhh!!”

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:03.760
“What did I do wrong?”

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:10.810
“Shhh…how many fingers am I holding up?”

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:15.020
“I don’t know, I don’t know?”

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:18.520
[Repeats process of shocking him]

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.630
John cries out.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:21.630
“How…many…fingers…am…I…holding…up?”

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:22.630
“Three?

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:23.630
Three?”

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:30.520
“I’m holding up as many fingers as I tell
your a$$ I’m holding up.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:35.980
Because it’s got nothing to do with your
eyes, nothing to do with your intellect or

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:37.540
your mind.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:45.990
When I say it’s three fingers, how many
are there?”

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:47.920
“Three!

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.850
Three!”

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:53.720
“Good boy.”

00:04:53.720 --> 00:05:05.630
Alternative facts…isn’t three an alternative
fact?

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:15.330
[Holds up four fingers].

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:21.440
You will believe what we tell you to believe,
nothing to do with your perspective at all.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:37.680
Okay…not me…what can

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.960
I say?

